### 1. Why the file tree failed

The `find` command used unescaped parentheses, which POSIX `/bin/sh` rejects:

```
find . -type f ( -name '*.ts' ... )      ← syntax error near `('
```

**Corrected command** (escape as `\(` `\)`, or run under bash/zsh):

```bash
find . -type f \( -name '*.ts' -o -name '*.tsx' -o -name '*.mjs' -o -name '*.js' -o -name '*.cjs' -o -name '*.jsx' -o -name '*.py' -o -name '*.java' -o -name '*.go' -o -name '*.rb' -o -name '*.php' \) \
  -not -path '*/node_modules/*' -not -path '*/.git/*' -not -path '*/.paaw/*' \
  -not -path '*/dist/*' -not -path '*/build/*' -not -path '*/coverage/*' \
  -not -path '*/data/semgrep-rules/*'
```

